\subsection*{1. Preliminaries}

Let $(\mathcal{M}, g_{\mu\nu})$ be a smooth four-dimensional manifold with
metric $g_{\mu\nu}$ and determinant $g$. The spectral field is defined as
\[
\Psi : \mathcal{M} \rightarrow \mathbb{C}.
\]

\begin{definition}[Spectral Gradient]
The spectral gradient of $\Psi$ is
\[
\nabla_\mu \Psi = \partial_\mu \Psi - \Gamma^\lambda_{\mu\lambda} \Psi,
\]
where $\Gamma^\lambda_{\mu\nu}$ denotes the Levi-Civita connection.
\end{definition}

